            <ArticleTitle>Incidental Intraductal Papillary Mucinous Neoplasm, Cystic or Premalignant Lesions of the Pancreas: The Case for Aggressive Management.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>141-155</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S0039-6109(17)30147-0</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.suc.2017.09.011</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Incidental cystic intrapancreatic lesions are daily findings in abdominal radiology. The discovery of incidental pancreatic lesions is increasingly common with technologic diagnostic advancements. This article provides a perspective and guideline on the clinical management of incidental intraductal papillary mucinous neoplasms and cystic or premalignant lesions of the pancreas.</AbstractText>
